    "updated_at": "2026-03-24T10:22:51Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the issue. Next time, please to fill the template in, as it can help define the scope of the problem and point to other solutions available today.\n\nWith that said, I don't think we should restore `<center>`. HTML is for semantics, not for visuals. There's no reason to have a `<center>` tag, just like there's not a reason for `<left>` `<right>` or `<justify>` tags. Those sorts of changes belong in CSS. The CSSWG resolved to allow `justify` & `align` properties inside block containers ([caniuse link](https://caniuse.com/wf-justify-self-block)) so centering a div is as simple as `<div style=\"justify-self:center\">centred</div>`. \n\nI'll leave this open for other vendors to comment but I propose we close as not-planned, unless any other vendor has other opinions.",
